      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-148037",
      ":question/problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$F(x, y) = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}x < 1ory < 1 \\\\ (4(x^{2} - 1)(y - 1))/(9y),\\end{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 2, 1 \\le y \\le 4; F_{X}(x),\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 2, y > 4 \\\\ F_{Y}(y),\\end{vmatrix}x > 2, 1 \\le y \\le 4; 1, \\mid x > 2, y > 4$.\n\nwhere $F_{X}$ and $F_{Y}$ are the marginal CDFs of $X$ and $Y$, respectively. Find the joint PDF $f(x, y)$ for $1 \\le x \\le 2$ and $1 \\le y \\le 4$."
